exports[`parsePerfGateArguments should document both commands and every configuration key 1`] = `
"Usage:
  npm run perf:gate -- measure --base-url <url> --out <file.json>
      [--only <configuration-key>]... [--passes <n>] [--commit <sha>]
      [--chrome-path <path>]
  npm run perf:gate -- compare --before <file.json> --after <file.json>
      [--bytes-ref <file.json>]

measure   Runs 12 configurations x --passes (default 5) Lighthouse passes against
          --base-url and writes per-configuration medians plus raw runs.
          With --only and an existing --out file, re-measures just those
          configurations and merges them in (the targeted rerun).
compare   Prints a Markdown pass/fail table; exits 1 if any check fails.

Configuration keys:
  mobile-light:/
  desktop-light:/
  mobile-light:/services/managed-it-services-ontario
  desktop-light:/services/managed-it-services-ontario
  mobile-light:/pricing
  desktop-light:/pricing
  mobile-light:/blog/backups
  desktop-light:/blog/backups
  mobile-dark:/
  mobile-dark:/pricing
  mobile-light-fonts-blocked:/
  mobile-light-fonts-blocked:/pricing

See docs/perf-gate.md for the before -> deploy -> after procedure."
`;
